// The application icon as Windows wants it.
//
// app.qrc carries the same drawing for the *window* -- that is what
// QIcon/setWindowIcon reads, and it is all Linux needs. Explorer, the taskbar
// button, the Alt-Tab list and any shortcut never look there: they read an
// ICON resource out of the .exe itself, and without this file there is none, so
// they fall back to the blank default executable icon.
//
// The id is 1 because the shell picks the ICON resource with the lowest
// numeric id as the application icon, and there must be no doubt about which
// one that is.
//
// newWe2002.ico is generated by tools/make_icon.py alongside the seven PNGs and
// holds the same seven drawings -- each drawn at its own size, not rescaled.
// rc.exe resolves the name relative to this file's directory.
//
// Compiled only on Windows; see src/app/CMakeLists.txt.

1 ICON "newWe2002.ico"
